{#
  traefik's bouncer-key precheck: refuse a key the CrowdSec LAPI rejects, before Traefik rolls
  (#6095).

  A rotation that skips `cscli bouncers delete k8straefik` leaves the LAPI holding the old
  key's hash. The new pod's startupProbe catches that through AppSec's 401, but traefik rolls
  `Recreate`, so by then no old pod serves. This directory renders into `traefik-precheck`,
  which `traefik` depends on and which copies traefik's edges, `crowdsec` among them. So the
  Job runs once the LAPI is Ready, and while it fails, Flux holds `traefik` and the old pod
  keeps serving. `backoffLimit: 0` keeps a failed check failed.

  It runs `files/traefik_bouncer_key_precheck.py`, whose docstring says why the request is a
  HEAD: a GET would add a `k8straefik@<pod IP>` row with a fresh `last_pull`, which
  `bouncer_prune.py` would read as the edge pulling.

  The key comes from the `traefik-precheck` Secret below, not from `traefik-crowdsec`: that
  Secret is in `traefik`, which has not applied when this Job runs. The Secret's placeholder
  makes `traefik-precheck` substitute from the cluster file. The spec embeds the key's
  `cluster-vars.source` digest, a digest of its ciphertext, so a rotation renames the Job and
  Flux runs it again. A Job that kept its name would satisfy `dependsOn` with the previous
  key's pass.

  DECIDED: the Job ships off, behind `traefik_k8s_bouncer_key_precheck`, and a second PR turns
  it on. Switched on in one PR with its fence peer, it deadlocks. The Job dials the LAPI
  through netpol-baseline's `networkpolicy-crowdsec.yaml.j2`, and netpol-baseline applies
  last, after `traefik`. Before the peer applies, the fence refuses the Job, the refused Job
  holds `traefik`, and a held `traefik` keeps netpol-baseline, and with it the peer, from
  applying. So the peer landed first, with the Job switched off (#6095). Setting the default
  to true is safe once netpol-baseline has applied the peer.

  The caller census (D5, *A fence admits every Job that dials through it*). The pod is
  `app: traefik-precheck` in `k8s_namespace`. It execs into nothing and dials one Service:
    - crowdsec:{{ crowdsec_k8s_lapi_port }}, the LAPI, through the LAPI fence in
      netpol-baseline's `networkpolicy-crowdsec.yaml.j2`, which lists `traefik-precheck` on
      the LAPI port alone. netpol-baseline's crowdsec row (`expect: refused`) shows that fence
      refuses an unlisted pod.
  Without the peer, the helper's 60 seconds of refused connects run out and the Job fails
  closed, naming the connect.
#}
{% set script_name = 'traefik_bouncer_key_precheck.py' %}
{% set script_dir = '/precheck' %}
{% set data = {
  script_name: lookup('file', playbook_dir + '/roles/k8s/traefik/files/' + script_name, rstrip=False),
  'flux_job_connect.py': flux_job_connect,
} %}
{% set configmap_name = 'traefik-precheck-' + ({'data': data, 'binaryData': {}} | to_json(sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':')) | hash('sha256'))[:8] %}
{#- The key's ciphertext digest, read from the cluster file's source; no value enters the
    spec. -#}
{% set key = namespace(digest='') %}
{% for line in lookup('file', playbook_dir + '/vars/cluster-vars.source').splitlines() if line and not line.startswith('#') and line.split()[0] == 'crowdsec_k8s_bouncer_api_key' %}
{% set key.digest = line.split()[1] %}
{% endfor %}
{% set spec_text %}
# No retry. A check that fails must not pass on its second try.
backoffLimit: 0
# One HEAD of 10s, plus the helper's 60s of connect retries, with slack.
activeDeadlineSeconds: 120
template:
  metadata:
    labels:
      app: traefik-precheck
  spec:
    serviceAccountName: traefik-precheck
    # The Job reads no Kubernetes API, so its pod holds no token.
    automountServiceAccountToken: false
    restartPolicy: Never
    enableServiceLinks: false
    securityContext:
      runAsNonRoot: true
      runAsUser: 65534
      runAsGroup: 65534
      seccompProfile:
        type: RuntimeDefault
    containers:
      - name: precheck
        image: {{ flux_job_image }}
        imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
        command:
          - python3
          - {{ script_dir }}/{{ script_name }}
        env:
          - name: LAPI_URL
            value: "http://crowdsec.{{ k8s_namespace }}.svc.cluster.local:{{ crowdsec_k8s_lapi_port }}"
          - name: BOUNCER_KEY
            valueFrom:
              secretKeyRef:
                name: traefik-precheck
                key: lapi_key
          # Renames the Job whenever the key rotates; see the note above.
          - name: BOUNCER_KEY_DIGEST
            value: "{{ key.digest }}"
          - name: PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE
            value: "1"
        resources:
          requests:
            cpu: 10m
            memory: 32Mi
          limits:
            memory: 64Mi
        securityContext:
          allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
          readOnlyRootFilesystem: true
          capabilities:
            drop:
              - ALL
        volumeMounts:
          - name: script
            mountPath: {{ script_dir }}
            readOnly: true
    volumes:
      - name: script
        configMap:
          name: {{ configmap_name }}
{% endset %}
{% set spec = spec_text | from_yaml %}
{% if traefik_k8s_bouncer_key_precheck | bool and traefik_k8s_manage_crowdsec | bool %}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: traefik-precheck
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
type: Opaque
stringData:
  lapi_key: "{{ crowdsec_k8s_bouncer_api_key }}"
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: {{ configmap_name }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
data:
{% for name, text in data | dictsort %}
  {{ name }}: {{ text | to_json }}
{% endfor %}
---
apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: Job
metadata:
  name: traefik-precheck-{{ (spec | to_json(sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':')) | hash('sha256'))[:8] }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
  annotations:
    # A read-only check that runs before `traefik` applies, the kind `traefik-precheck` admits.
    homelab/job-kind: precheck
spec:
{{ spec_text | indent(2, true) }}
{% endif %}
